# deadcode.baseline — known-unreachable functions accepted by `make deadcode`.
#
# `golang.org/x/tools/cmd/deadcode` reports functions unreachable from the
# `nrflo_server` and `nrflo` main packages. The entries below are unreachable
# from those entry points but are NOT dead, for one of these reasons:
#
#   * test infrastructure — used only by *_test.go (deadcode does not treat
#     per-package tests as roots): clock.NewTest / TestClock.*, ws.NewTestClient,
#     db.Open*/*PoolExisting, repo CRUD exercised directly by tests, etc.
#   * socket / reflection dispatch — reached by name over the unix socket or via
#     interface dispatch the static call graph cannot see: api.getAgentSession.
#   * spawner.ConsoleEngine + codexEngine.* — the console-session driver, fully
#     covered by console_engine_*_test.go; its production caller is the sessions
#     service, which is not wired to a server entry point yet.
#
# `make deadcode` fails only on NEW unreachable funcs (present in the analysis
# but absent here). When you delete code, also delete its line(s) below.
# Format: "<package import path> <FuncName | Type.Method>", sorted.
#
be/internal/api getAgentSession
be/internal/client NewWithAddr
be/internal/clock NewTest
be/internal/clock TestClock.Advance
be/internal/clock TestClock.After
be/internal/clock TestClock.fireTimers
